# PHASE 5 — COMPREHENSIVE PRODUCT INFORMATION

Customers should not need to message the owner just to discover basic product specifications.

Every product detail page should have a clear, organised information section.

Support the following fields:

### Product identity
- Product name.
- Category.
- Product description.
- Product code or SKU, where used.

### Price
- Base price in NGN.
- International currency display, when supported.
- Clear pricing for variations if prices genuinely differ.

### Product origin
- Country of manufacture or origin, when confirmed.
- Supplier or collection origin, if relevant and approved.

Never assume a garment is made in Dubai, Egypt, Nigeria, Turkey or any other country simply because of its style.

### Material and fabric
- Fabric type.
- Texture.
- Thickness or weight, if known.
- Transparency or lining information, if known.
- Care instructions, if supplied.

Do not invent material claims.

### Product construction
Where relevant, show:
- Sleeve style.
- Neckline.
- Closure type.
- Hood or attached veil.
- Embroidery.
- Pockets.
- Included accessories.
- Other genuine design features.

### Product contents

Clearly explain what is included in the purchase.

For example, if an item includes an Abaya only, say so.

If it includes an Abaya and matching veil, state that.

Do not allow customers to assume accessories in a photograph are included when they are not.

### Availability
- Available colours.
- Available sizes.
- Actual stock status.
- Availability of each variation.

Do not display fabricated product specifications.

If information has not been supplied, omit it or show a clear neutral message such as "Contact the store for details."

