# PHASE 12 — REAL ORDER MANAGEMENT AND CUSTOMER NOTIFICATIONS

The customer specifically requested a system that informs her when an order has been received, processed, dispatched and delivered.

Implement a proper order-management workflow.

## 12.1 Order records

If the current WhatsApp checkout only sends a message and does not create an order record, improve the architecture so that the customer can submit an order request and the store can record and manage it.

Do not mark an order as confirmed merely because a customer opened WhatsApp.

Where the business workflow requires owner confirmation, make that distinction clear.

Create or improve the existing Supabase order records to support:

- Unique order reference.
- Customer details.
- Ordered products.
- Selected variations.
- Quantities.
- Product prices at the time of ordering.
- Order subtotal.
- Delivery information.
- Order status.
- Order creation date.
- Status update timestamps.
- Tracking reference, where available.

Preserve historical order information even if a product is later edited or deleted.

## 12.2 Order statuses

Support an appropriate order lifecycle:

1. Order received.
2. Awaiting confirmation.
3. Confirmed.
4. Processing.
5. Ready for dispatch.
6. Dispatched.
7. Out for delivery.
8. Delivered.
9. Cancelled.
10. Returned, where the business supports returns.

The admin must be able to update the order status.

Each status change must persist in Supabase.

Do not display a false delivered status.

## 12.3 Customer order tracking

Provide a secure customer-facing way to check order progress.

This may use a secure order reference and an appropriate verification mechanism.

Do not expose one customer's address, phone number, order history or personal information to another customer.

The tracking page should clearly display:

- Order reference.
- Order date.
- Current status.
- Status timeline.
- Dispatch information.
- Delivery information, where available.

## 12.4 Email notifications

Support email notifications for relevant order events:

- Order received.
- Order confirmed.
- Order dispatched.
- Out for delivery, where supported.
- Order delivered.

Use a suitable email service and secure server-side configuration.

Do not hardcode email API secrets into the frontend.

Do not claim emails have been sent unless the email service confirms successful delivery or acceptance.

If no email provider is configured, build the integration safely and document the exact configuration required.

## 12.5 Delivery confirmation

Delivery should be recorded only when the store or delivery provider confirms it.

Where the delivery provider offers tracking integration, use it only if the provider supports the required API.

If no integration exists, allow the authorised admin to update delivery status manually and record who made the update and when.

The customer should then receive the appropriate notification.

